DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((x^2))");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^((ln(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-5, -4, 0, 2, 8} U [2, infinity) U [2, infinity)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-4, -3} U (([2, infinity)) U [2, infinity))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(({-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7} U ({-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7} U {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7}))) U (({-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7})) U {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7} U (({-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7}) U {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7} U {-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7}))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7}) U {-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`17+5-1-15`]? [_____]{6}
---

What is the value of [`3+16-15*12`]? [_____]{Real(-161.)}
---

What is the value of [`12+14*5`]? [_____]{Formula('82')}
---

[`16*19+17/1`] is equal to [_____]{Real(321.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-5, -4, -3, 0, 4, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -7, -3, -1, 2, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B \cup (B \cup A \cap A) \cap A) \cap (A)) \cup ((A)) \cup A \cup ((B) \cup A \cup B \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-4, -3\}`]
- [`B = \{-5, -4, 0, 2, 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup ((C) \cup C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, 1, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, 7, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, 7, 1>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 1, 4>") . Compute("<4, 7, 1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<4, 7, 1>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, 1, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 1, 4>") x Compute("<4, 7, 1>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, 1, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 0, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 0, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 1, 8>") . Compute("<2, 0, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 0, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 1, 8>") x Compute("<2, 0, -8>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>0)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
